/**
 * @mainpage Skip List (C++20)
 *
 * @section intro_sec 📚 Introduction
 *
 * This project is a modern, generic implementation of a Skip List data structure written in C++20.  
 * It supports STL-style features and uses C++20 concepts (`requires std::totally_ordered<T>`) for strict type checking.
 *
 * @section features_sec 🚀 Features
 * - Template-based skip list: SkipList<T>
 * - STL-style forward iterator:
 *   - begin(), end() for range-based loops
 * - Core container operations:
 *   - insert, erase, find
 * - Container utilities:
 *   - size(), empty(), clear(), swap(), operator[]
 * - Equality operators: ==, !=
 * - Uses C++20 concepts: requires std::totally_ordered<T>
 * - Fully unit tested using Google Test
 * - Doxygen-compatible documentation
 *
 * @section example_sec 📎 Example
 *
 * @code{.cpp}
 * #include "skip_list.hpp"
 * #include <iostream>
 *
 * int main() {
 *     SkipList<int> list;
 *     list.insert(10);
 *     list.insert(20);
 *
 *     if (list.find(10)) {
 *         std::cout << "Found 10!" << std::endl;
 *     }
 *
 *     for (const auto& item : list) {
 *         std::cout << item << " ";
 *     }
 *     std::cout << std::endl;
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section usage_sec 🧪 Running Tests
 * Make sure you have GoogleTest installed. Then simply run:
 * @code{.bash}
 * make test
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section doc_sec 📘 Full Documentation
 * The full documentation includes:
 * - Class and member function reference
 * - Iterator usage
 * - Concept constraints and requirements
 *
 * You can generate the HTML docs by:
 * @code{.bash}
 * cd docs
 * doxygen Doxyfile
 * @endcode
 * Then open docs/html/index.html in your browser.
 *
 * @section license_sec 📄 License
 * This project is licensed under the MIT License. See the LICENSE file.
 *
 * @section author Author
 * Created by [Mokobia Joan Chidiebere], 2025.
 */